Include <cstdint> in semver.h, which uses uint32_t without it.

GCC 13 stopped providing <cstdint> transitively through other standard headers
and GCC 16 enforces that, so the build fails with "'uint32_t' does not name a
type". Older toolchains -- including the gcc-toolset-14 CI uses -- happen to
pull it in indirectly and never notice.

Only bites when onnxruntime is built from source; CI pulls it from the vcpkg
binary cache.

diff --git a/onnxruntime/core/common/semver.h b/onnxruntime/core/common/semver.h
index a07c24f..98bb6a2 100644
--- a/onnxruntime/core/common/semver.h
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/common/semver.h
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <optional>
 #include <string_view>
 
